<%--
Pin_Input

A one-value input for a short numeric code, rendered as N single-character boxes.
Its value is the whole code as a string ('' when nothing is entered) - the boxes are
presentation, not separate fields.

  $name    (required) the field name the form serializes it under
  $length  number of digits (default 6)

  <Form_Field $label="Verification code" $required=true>
      <Pin_Input $name="pin" $length=6 />
  </Form_Field>

Interaction: typing a digit advances, Backspace on an empty box clears and steps back,
the arrow keys move, and a paste distributes its digits across the boxes.

There is NO "you must enter all N digits" check here. Completeness is a rule the SERVER
can see for itself, so it lives there once - a client copy of it would hide the day the
server's copy went missing (see Rsx_Form's docblock).
--%>
<Define:Pin_Input extends="Form_Input_Abstract" tag="div">
    <div class="Pin_Input__boxes d-flex justify-content-center gap-2" $sid="boxes">
        <% const _length = this.args.length ? int(this.args.length) : 6; %>
        <% for (let i = 0; i < _length; i++) { %>
            <input type="text" class="form-control Pin_Input__box text-center"
                maxlength="1" inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]" autocomplete="off"
                data-index="<%= i %>" />
        <% } %>
    </div>
</Define:Pin_Input>
